"""The contract-faithful PDM oracle for direct T4 scenes.

The default trajectory contract predicts 8 poses at 0.5 s intervals. The
scorer evaluates every proposal by converting it to a 10 Hz
``nuPlan`` trajectory, running the original PDM bicycle/LQR simulator, and
calling the scorer. This module keeps
that exact boundary while replacing only the dataset-side objects:

* T4 ego shape and current dynamics become a nuPlan ``EgoState``;
* T4 future boxes become the original ``PDMObservation``;
* T4 lanes/route/polygons become the original ``PDMPath`` and
  ``PDMDrivableMap``.

There is deliberately no trajectory-closeness label, no proxy metric,
``pdms_proxy``, and no learned/GPU approximation in the formal path.  The
oracle is detached from autograd, just as the original metric-cache scorer
was during cache generation.
"""

